CM_ BO_ 0 "Also pushed immediately on any axis.error_ change (BSR v3.7), not just on the heartbeat_rate_ms timer.";
CM_ BO_ 28 "Request (Master->axis) is 1 byte: GPIO_Num (uint8) at byte 0. Response (shown here) is the ADC voltage reading.";
CM_ BO_ 30 "BSR v3.7 custom. Nonzero enables the DRV8301 PWRGD gate-driver-fault check for this axis.";
CM_ BO_ 31 "BSR v3.7 custom, request AND response share this id/layout. Generic read/write of any Fibre property or function by its numeric endpoint id (same ids USB/UART use) - see CANSimple::endpoint_op_callback() in can_simple.cpp. The 'Value' field's actual meaning depends entirely on which endpoint id is addressed and cannot be described generically here; empty (2-byte message) = read, present = write-then-read-back. 64-bit endpoints don't fit and are not reachable this way.";
CM_ BO_ 32 "Also pushed immediately on any axis.error_ change (BSR v3.7), not just on the heartbeat_rate_ms timer.";
CM_ BO_ 60 "Request (Master->axis) is 1 byte: GPIO_Num (uint8) at byte 0. Response (shown here) is the ADC voltage reading.";
CM_ BO_ 62 "BSR v3.7 custom. Nonzero enables the DRV8301 PWRGD gate-driver-fault check for this axis.";
CM_ BO_ 63 "BSR v3.7 custom, request AND response share this id/layout. Generic read/write of any Fibre property or function by its numeric endpoint id (same ids USB/UART use) - see CANSimple::endpoint_op_callback() in can_simple.cpp. The 'Value' field's actual meaning depends entirely on which endpoint id is addressed and cannot be described generically here; empty (2-byte message) = read, present = write-then-read-back. 64-bit endpoints don't fit and are not reachable this way.";
CM_ BO_ 1040 "BSR v3.7 custom MIT-mode command frame - NOT part of the node_id<<5|cmd_id scheme, this is its own dedicated arbitration id (Axis.config.can.mit_can_id). Raw values are packed 16/12/12/12/12-bit fixed point; decode with the ranges configured in Axis.config.can.mit_*_min/max (see Firmware/docs/MIT_MODE_BSR.md). Standard cantools scaling can't express 'range depends on runtime config', so this DBC only documents bit positions/widths, not physical units - decode the raw ints and apply the ODrive-side range yourself (or read them back over USB/UART/CAN-endpoint-op to confirm).";
CM_ SG_ 1040 Torque_FF_Raw "12-bit fixed point over [mit_torque_min, mit_torque_max]";
CM_ SG_ 1040 Kd_Raw "12-bit fixed point over [mit_kd_min, mit_kd_max]";
CM_ SG_ 1040 Kp_Raw "12-bit fixed point over [mit_kp_min, mit_kp_max]";
CM_ SG_ 1040 Vel_Des_Raw "12-bit fixed point over [mit_vel_min, mit_vel_max]";
CM_ SG_ 1040 Pos_Des_Raw "16-bit fixed point over [mit_pos_min, mit_pos_max] - see MIT_MODE_BSR.md";
CM_ BO_ 1041 "BSR v3.7 custom MIT-mode reply frame, sent on Axis.config.can.mit_reply_can_id after each command.";
